From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: recover unresponsive IPC after warm reboot

The firmware can remain loaded across a warm reboot while its IPC interface
is no longer responsive. In that case the model-specific driver matches,
but its probe times out while synchronizing IPC parity.

On an IPC synchronization timeout, reset the PHY, reload its firmware and
retry synchronization. Issue a NOP command to wait for the freshly loaded
firmware to become ready and report successful recovery in the boot log.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -606,6 +606,7 @@ static int aeon_dpc_ra_enable(struct phy
 static int as21xxx_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	struct as21xxx_priv *priv;
+	u16 ret_sts;
 	int ret;
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(&phydev->mdio.dev,
@@ -627,6 +628,28 @@ static int as21xxx_probe(struct phy_devi
 	phydev->c45_ids.devices_in_package &= ~BIT(0);
 
 	ret = aeon_ipc_sync_parity(phydev, priv);
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		phydev_warn(phydev,
+			    "Aeonsemi recovery: IPC unresponsive, resetting PHY\n");
+
+		phy_device_reset(phydev, 1);
+		phy_device_reset(phydev, 0);
+
+		ret = aeon_firmware_load(phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		priv->parity_status = false;
+		ret = aeon_ipc_sync_parity(phydev, priv);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		/* Wait for the freshly loaded firmware to become ready. */
+		ret = aeon_ipc_noop(phydev, priv, &ret_sts);
+		if (!ret)
+			phydev_info(phydev,
+				    "Aeonsemi recovery: IPC reset and firmware reload succeeded\n");
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
